From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
Subject: [PATCH] Add CPL_CPUID guard for AVX2 runtime detection

The HAVE_AVX2_AT_COMPILE_TIME code path in
port/cpl_cpu_features.cpp calls __builtin_cpu_supports("avx2"),
which is not supported on non-x86 targets (including
wasm32-unknown-emscripten) and fails to compile with:

    error: builtin is not supported on this target
        bCPLHasAVX2 = CPLHaveRuntimeAVX() && __builtin_cpu_supports("avx2");

Mirrors the SSE/SSSE3/AVX handling in
0001-Add-CPL_CPUID-guards.patch: gate the CPUID-dependent block on
defined(CPL_CPUID) and provide a fallback that leaves bCPLHasAVX2
as false on non-x86 builds.
---
 port/cpl_cpu_features.cpp | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/port/cpl_cpu_features.cpp b/port/cpl_cpu_features.cpp
--- a/port/cpl_cpu_features.cpp
+++ b/port/cpl_cpu_features.cpp
@@ -216,7 +216,7 @@ bool CPLHaveRuntimeAVX()

 #if defined(HAVE_AVX2_AT_COMPILE_TIME) && !defined(HAVE_INLINE_AVX2)

-#if defined(__GNUC__)
+#if defined(__GNUC__) && defined(CPL_CPUID)

 bool bCPLHasAVX2 = false;
 // Use 102 because  CPLHaveRuntimeAVXInitialize() uses 101, so we are run
@@ -228,6 +228,10 @@ static void CPLHaveRuntimeAVX2Initialize()
     bCPLHasAVX2 = CPLHaveRuntimeAVX() && __builtin_cpu_supports("avx2");
 }

+#elif defined(__GNUC__) && !defined(CPL_CPUID)
+
+bool bCPLHasAVX2 = false;
+
 #else

 /************************************************************************/
</content>
